# Official Language!

## Nehru's Reply to Members of Parliament

New Delhi, August 4: In his reply to a letter signed and sent by fifteen opposition Members of Parliament, Prime Minister Nehru has said that what he stated in Parliament reflects his government's policy and that there need be no doubt about it. Nehru has assured them that English, along with Hindi, will remain an associate language of administration for as long as non-Hindi-speaking people desire it.

In his letter, Nehru noted that the President had also made this clear in his Hyderabad speech.

Mr. N. Sivaraj, one of the Members of Parliament who signed the letter sent to Nehru, released Nehru's reply to the press. The letter states:

"Dear friends,

"I have received your letter dated August 3 concerning the order issued by the President on the language question. Two days ago, the Home Minister made a statement in the Lok Sabha that what I said in the House is the policy of the government and that the government will adhere to it. The President too explained this in his Hyderabad speech. Therefore, there need be no doubt of any kind about it. The government is wholly bound to act according to the decision and the policy adopted. There should be no misunderstanding or difference of opinion about it."

Jawaharlal Nehru

(*Dravida Nadu*, news item, 14-8-60)
